# FIXED 2026-08-29 (RECURSION.0.md P0: same()/valSame compare
# spreads, and a literal list alternative admits only its own length
# -- list_length). `v: oops` below now refuses as empty at the
# list, the refusal a disjunct can state; kept as the regime-4
# record.
# 52 (regime 4): the recursive spelling that "works" checks NOTHING --
# the well-formed wrong config shape. `v: oops` should refuse against
# `v: integer`; instead the whole tree generates at any depth with the
# schema silently unapplied below the root.
#
# run: node ../../../ts/bin/aontu.js spread-template-never-applies.aon
# run: aontu-go spread-template-never-applies.aon
#
# expected: [aontu/no_scalar_unify] (or kin) at $.t.kids.0.v
# actual (both ports): {"t":{"kids":[{"kids":[],"v":"oops"}],"v":1}}
#
# The disjunct admits the `[&: $.Node]` branch wholesale and the
# spread template inside it is never applied to the elements --
# consistent with edge.tsv:edge-spread-disjunct-key, but reached here
# from a schema an author would write in good faith. A missing `v`
# passes the same way.
Node: hide({v: integer, kids: [] | [&: $.Node]})
t: $.Node & {v: 1, kids: [{v: oops, kids: []}]}
